            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Introduction\n\nIn this text, we will examine a different way of multiplying that the Maya may have used (<htcite0>; <htcite1>). As with addition, we cannot be certain how these calculations were performed, because no written record describes their methods.\n\nBecause their methods differed from ours, they raise the following reflection:",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "38f05ff2-70fd-43da-bf0e-34a6315171c5",
                     "text": "Díaz, Ruy D.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ced67eaf-7378-4589-9166-07f799969e3e",
                     "text": "Catepillán, Ximena",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2023",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 1: On methodology</b><br /><br />If we multiply in a completely different way, can the result be different?</div></div></center>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_common",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### A Common Conclusion\n\nDescribing the multiplication performed by the Maya, Dr. Ximena Catepillán suggests that, for small numbers, Indigenous peoples possibly obtained the product by repeating a number a given number of times (<htcite0>). This is the very idea behind Dhavit Prem's *\"Yupana Inka Tawa Pukllay\"* method (<htcite1>; <htcite2>), which we studied earlier (<htcite3>): multiplication is repeated addition.\n\nWe revisit the idea in **Table 1**. Choose two values between 0 and 9, then select **Values** to place them on the *Yupana*, or **Calculations** to build the product one repeated addition at a time:",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ced67eaf-7378-4589-9166-07f799969e3e",
                     "text": "Catepillán, Ximena",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2023",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a62b520a-f443-4d83-ab51-b99c9a46dab8",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "pp. 354 - 363",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "2d2ea4a5-506b-4dbf-aaa4-3a10a8fbbd9c",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "c4c2c00d-7878-42da-9cc4-060cd7f8d225",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Yupana (multiplication)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p style=\"margin: auto; with: 50%;\"><input type=\"number\" value=\"7\" min=\"0\" max=\"9\" id=\"ia2yupana0\" /> × <input type=\"number\" value=\"8\" min=\"0\" max=\"9\" id=\"ia2yupana1\" />:  <input type=\"radio\" value=\"values\" name=\"yupanaradio\" /> <b>Values</b> <input type=\"radio\" value=\"calcular\" name=\"yupanaradio\" /> <b>Calculations</b></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"yupana0\" class=\"tawapukllay\"><tr><th colspan=\"4\"><i>Yupana</i></th><th>Values</th><th>Results</th><th>Movements</th></tr> <tr id=\"tf1\"><td id=\"tc1f1\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f1\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f1\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f1\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td><td id=\"tc5f1\"><span id=\"vl1\"></span> x <span id=\"vr1\"></span></td><td id=\"tc6f1\">&nbsp;</td><td id=\"tc7f1\" rowspan=\"5\">&nbsp;</td></tr> <tr id=\"tf2\"><td id=\"tc1f2\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f2\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f2\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f2\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td><td id=\"tc5f2\"><span id=\"vl2\"></span> x <span id=\"vr2\"></span></td><td id=\"tc6f2\">&nbsp;</td></tr> <tr id=\"tf3\"><td id=\"tc1f3\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f3\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f3\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f3\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td><td id=\"tc5f3\"><span id=\"vl3\"></span> x <span id=\"vr3\"></span></td><td id=\"tc6f3\">&nbsp;</td></tr> <tr id=\"tf4\"><td id=\"tc1f4\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f4\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f4\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f4\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td><td id=\"tc5f4\"><span id=\"vl4\"></span> x <span id=\"vr4\"></span></td><td id=\"tc6f4\">&nbsp;</td></tr> <tr id=\"tf5\"><td id=\"tc1f5\"><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_center\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c1_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_up\"></span><span class=\"dot five_dot_c2_bottom\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc2f5\"><span class=\"dot three_dot_bottom\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_up\"></span><span class=\"dot three_dot_center\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc3f5\"><span class=\"dot two_dot_bottom\"></span> <span class=\"dot two_dot_up\"></span></td> <td id=\"tc4f5\"><span class=\"dot dot_center\"></span></td><td id=\"tc5f5\"><span id=\"vl5\"></span> x <span id=\"vr5\"></span></td><td id=\"tc6f5\">&nbsp;</td></tr></table>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "The Yupana consists of a table with four columns and five rows: The first column contains five circles; The second column has three circles; The third column has two circles; The last column contains only one circle; This pattern repeats across all rows. Adjacent to the Yupana, we have added two columns showing conventional numerical representations. Finally, we included a column describing all the summation steps performed to obtain the final result.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><b>Table 1</b>: Representation of the <i>Yupana</i> according to Poma de Ayala (<htcite0>; <htcite1>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a62b520a-f443-4d83-ab51-b99c9a46dab8",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "pp. 355,",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2018",
                        "month": "04",
                        "day": "01"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "f5b74f18-0bc4-46d2-8a5c-64dd80b74dd1",
                     "text": "Poma de Ayala, Felipe Guaman",
                     "page": "pp. 361 - 362,",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "1615",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "13"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "2018",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  },
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "1615",
                     "month": "-1",
                     "day": "-1"
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_maya_step",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Multiplying with Grids\n\nWe cannot be certain that the Mesoamericans used grids to multiply, but neither can we dismiss the evidence that points to this possibility (<htcite0>; <htcite1>). In this section we follow the work of Ruy D. Díaz and Ximena Catepillán and repeat their operations step by step.\n\nWe begin with only two numerical orders, *K’iin* (our units) and *Winal* (our tens), and compute **21 × 42 = 882**. Every number written on the grid is one of these two factors.\n\n#### Understanding the Grid\n\nFirst, we set up a grid in the following format (<htcite2>):",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "38f05ff2-70fd-43da-bf0e-34a6315171c5",
                     "text": "Díaz, Ruy D.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ced67eaf-7378-4589-9166-07f799969e3e",
                     "text": "Catepillán, Ximena",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2023",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ced67eaf-7378-4589-9166-07f799969e3e",
                     "text": "Catepillán, Ximena",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2023",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"emptyGrid\" class=\"tableTen\"> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\">&nbsp;</td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>Second order</b></td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>First order</b></td></tr>  <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>Second order</b></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>First order</b></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr> </table></p> <p class=\"desc\">Table 2 – multiplication grid.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "It is important to see how the orders are arranged: the higher orders meet in the upper-left corner, and each lower order steps one cell down and to the right. As a result, the cells that lie on the same diagonal always produce values of the same order — which is exactly why we can add along the diagonals later. To make the layout clearer, here is the multiplication we are performing (**21 × 42**) in decimal format:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"decGrid\" class=\"tableTen\"> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\">&nbsp;</td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>4</b></td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>2</b></td></tr>  <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>2</b></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>1</b></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr> </table></p> <p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 1</b>: Multiplication of 21 by 42.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### Writing in the Grid\n\nBecause this is a Mesoamerican method, we now rewrite those same digits in Mesoamerican notation before going on:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"decGrid\" class=\"tableTen\"> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\">&nbsp;</td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><img id=\"imgt00\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgt00', '0%')\"  /></td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><img id=\"imgt10\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgt10', '0%')\"  /></td></tr>  <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b><img id=\"imgl00\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl00', '0%')\"  /></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><img id=\"imgl10\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl10', '0%')\"  /></td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td></tr> </table></p> <p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 2</b>: Multiplication of 21 by 42.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### Multiplying\n\nBefore we see how the Maya may have carried out the operation, let us recall how multiplication works in our own system (<htcite0>):",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "4ee22ab8-e17c-48a8-8289-c8538aba77bf",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Rereading",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p style=\"text-align=center\"><center>Multiplication by: <input class=\"ordercheck\" type=\"checkbox\" id=\"1\" /> Units <input class=\"ordercheck\" type=\"checkbox\" id=\"2\" /> Tens</center></p><p style=\"text-align=center\"><center>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmtc2\">2 </span><span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmtc1\">1 </span> <br />× &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmbc2\">4 </span><span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmbc1\">2 </span><br />_________<br /></span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmptrc2\">4 </span><span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmptrc1\">2 </span><br />+ <span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmpbrc3\">8 </span><span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmpbrc2\">4 </span><span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmpbrc1\">0 </span><br />_________<br />&nbsp; <span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmrc3\">8 </span><span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmrc2\">8 </span><span class=\"multexample1\" id=\"mmrc1\">2 </span></center></p><p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 3</b>: Multiplication of 21 by 42.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "In **Calculation 3** we first multiply 21 by the units digit (2) and then by the tens digit (4, which stands for 40) — a shortcut often described as *\"multiplying by 4 and adding a zero.\"* The grid does the same thing, only in two directions at once: each square multiplies the order on its row by the order on its column, and the product lands in that square. Use the arrow <i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrow-right\" style=\"color:#0f0;\"></i> to advance one multiplication at a time, and the arrow <i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate\" style=\"color:#00f;\"></i> to restart:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"decGrid\" class=\"tableTen\"> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\">&nbsp;</td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><img id=\"imgt0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgt0', '0%')\"  /></td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><img id=\"imgt1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgt1', '0%')\"  /></td><td><b>Controls</b></td></tr>  <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b><img id=\"imgl0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl0', '0%')\"  /></td><td><img id=\"imgm3\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgm3', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"imgm1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgm1', '0%')\" /></td><td rowspan=\"2\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrow-right upArrowWithFA\" id=\"traineeUp3\"></i> <i class=\"fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate downArrowWithFA\" style=\"font-size:4em;color:#00f;\" id=\"traineeDown3\"></i></td></tr> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><img id=\"imgl1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl1', '0%')\"  /></td><td><img id=\"imgm2\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgm2', '0%')\" /></td><td><img id=\"imgm0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgm0', '0%')\" /></td></tr> </table></p> <p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 4</b>: Multiplication of 21 by 42.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "In the Maya grid, the multiplications do not have to be carried out in the same order as in the decimal method. We kept that order here only to make it easier to see which numbers were multiplied.\n\n#### Repositioning\n\nNow we read the grid along its diagonals and add the values that fall on each one. Because each diagonal gathers products of the same order, the sums line up place by place. To make this easier to follow, **Calculation 5** repeats **Calculation 4** with the diagonals shaded in different colors:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"decGrid\" class=\"tableTen\"> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\">&nbsp;</td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><img id=\"imgt000\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgt000', '0%')\"  /></td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><img id=\"imgt100\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgt100', '0%')\"  /></td></tr>  <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b><img id=\"imgl000\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl000', '0%')\"  /></td><td style=\"background-color: lightyellow\"><img id=\"imgm300\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgm300', '0%')\"  /></td><td style=\"background-color: lightgreen\"><img id=\"imgm100\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgm100', '0%')\"  /></td></tr> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><img id=\"imgl100\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl100', '0%')\"  /></td><td style=\"background-color: lightgreen\"><img id=\"imgm200\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgm200', '0%')\"  /></td><td style=\"background-color: lightgray\"><img id=\"imgm000\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgm000', '0%')\"  /></td></tr> </table></p> <p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 5</b>: Multiplication of 21 by 42.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "Finally, we add each diagonal and obtain the result:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><table id=\"decGrid\" class=\"tableTen\"> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\">&nbsp;</td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>Separating order</b></td><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>Result</b></td></tr>  <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>Third order</td><td style=\"background-color: lightyellow\"><img id=\"imgl00000\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl00000', '0%')\"  /></td><td style=\"background-color: lightyellow\"><img id=\"imgl00000\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl00000', '0%')\"  /></td></tr> <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>Second order</b></td><td style=\"background-color: lightgreen\"><img id=\"imgl10000\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl10000', '0%')\"  /> + <img id=\"imgl10000\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl10000', '0%')\"  /></td><td style=\"background-color: lightgreen\"><img id=\"imgl10000\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl10000', '0%')\" /></td></tr>  <tr><td style=\"background-color: lightblue\"><b>First order</b></td><td style=\"background-color: lightgray\"><img id=\"imgl10000\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl10000', '0%')\"  /></td><td style=\"background-color: lightgray\"><img id=\"imgl10000\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgl10000', '0%')\"  /></td></tr> </table></p> <p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 6</b>: Multiplication of 21 by 42.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 2: On Calculation 6</b><br /><br />Is the result shown in Calculation 6 correct?</div></div></center>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### Confirming the Result\n\nThe additions and the multiplication in **Calculation 6** are correct, and the three results there stand for three numerical orders. To confirm the value **882** obtained in **Calculation 3**, let us make those orders explicit and add them up:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\" style=\"background-color: #FFFFFF;\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\" style=\"background-color: #FFFFFF;\"><p style=\"text-align=center\"><p><math mathsize=\"1.5em\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mn>882</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">= (</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">×</mo><mn>400</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">) + </mo><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">×</mo><mn>20</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">) + </mo><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">)</mo></math></p> <p><math mathsize=\"1.5em\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mn>882</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">= (</mo><mn>800</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">) + </mo><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">(</mo><mn>80</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">) + </mo><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">)</mo></math></p>  <p><math mathsize=\"1.5em\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mn>882</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">= (</mo><mn>800</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">) + </mo><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">(</mo><mn>82</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">)</mo></math></p> <p><math mathsize=\"1.5em\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mn>882</mn><mo lspace=\"0.1667em\" rspace=\"0.1667em\">= </mo><mn>882</mn></math></p>  <p class=\"desc\"><b>Calculation 7</b>: Rewriting 882 to show its numerical orders in the vigesimal base.</p></div></div></center>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 3: On Calculation 7</b><br /><br />Calculation 7 confirmed the result of Calculation 3. So there is nothing left to check, right?</div></div></center>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "If the number of verifications seemed excessive, do not worry: checking your work is part of learning, and we will keep being asked to justify our understanding.\n\nOne caveat still matters. Everything above used the **vigesimal** system, in which each order multiplies the previous one by 20. There is no evidence that the Mesoamericans used a system in exactly this way (<htcite0>; <htcite1>; <htcite2>). The Maya numerical system was the **calendrical** one, which we explored in the previous text (<htcite3>): there the third order multiplies by 18, not by 20.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "ad11b3b2-8cdf-4d71-9cb7-2ac241850945",
                     "text": "Casares Contreras, Orlando & Cetina, José & Cabrera, Venus Sarahí.",
                     "page": "pp. 34",
