         "id": "SECTION_conclusion",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Conclusion\n\nIn this text, we studied the Mesoamerican grid and how the Maya might have used it to multiply. Two ideas made it work: every square multiplies the orders that meet there, and every diagonal gathers products of the same order.\n\nThis is the last text about calendars in this chapter. In the next one, we will look more closely at the divisions of the calendar and explore another mathematical operation with Mesoamerican numbers: division.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      }
